@startuml physical
!include style.iuml
top to bottom direction
title LazyFinance — Development Deployment\n<color:#1E40AF>STAGE C · CONFIGURED DEVELOPMENT TOPOLOGY</color>

node "<b>Browser</b>\nAngular private CSR / public prerender" as Browser <<boundary>>
node "External MCP client" as Client <<external client>>

node " " as Host {
  node "<b>Traefik · edge</b>\nHTTPS :443 / redirect :80\nACME certificates" as Edge <<boundary>>
  node "<b>Static Nginx UI :4000</b>\nedge · no API proxy" as UI <<boundary>>
  node "<b>NestJS API :3000</b>\nedge + services\nFirebase; demo tools enabled" as API <<application>>
  node "<b>Private persistence :3001</b>\nservices + data\nRestricted runtime and dedicated demo logins" as Persistence <<persistence>>
  database "<b>PostgreSQL 18 :5432</b>\ndata · postgres-data volume" as DB
  artifact "<b>One-shot init · data</b>\nMigrate / provision runtime and demo logins" as Init
}

component "<b>External providers</b>\nFirebase Auth · Fintoc test mode\nConfigured model / optional Realtime" as Providers <<adapter>>

Browser --> Edge : HTTPS UI and API origins
Client --> Edge : HTTPS OAuth / MCP
Edge --> UI : configured WEB_DOMAIN
Edge --> API : api.lazyfinance.online
API --> Persistence : signed HTTP tRPC
Persistence --> DB : scoped SQL
Init ..> DB : owner-only before runtime
API ..> Providers

legend bottom
  The shaded box is the development host (docker/dev/compose.yml).
  Only Traefik publishes host ports; services and data are internal networks.
  The browser calls the API origin directly. Provider SDK / Widget and optional browser WebRTC traffic are not drawn.
  Automatic bank sync is off. The opt-in seed job is not part of deployment, and the persistent volume is not a backup.
  Stage C development configuration, not production release evidence.
endlegend
@enduml
